oliver: Opening a small PR to consolidate our tool-calling + structured output docs — aiming to: 1) add a migration note for JSON schema guards, 2) include concise Python/JS SDK snippets, 3) fix a couple broken links. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1756 :partyparrot:
sana: thank you! can you add a short migration section for older prompts that relied on regex parsing? most customers need guidance on switching to schema validation without breaking flows
keith: also call out the difference between 'tool' vs 'function' naming in SDKs — we've had users confused by that in support tickets. small snippet that shows both would help
oliver: good call. plan: a short subsection "From regex to JSON Schema" + examples. for SDKs i'll add two tiny snippets (python + js) showing function/tool call with 'json_schema' + fallback parsing. keeping them intentionally minimal
andrea: please also add a note about streaming responses — when structured output is used with streaming the final JSON may be truncated; recommend using full_response buffer or post-process reassemble. file an issue link to runtime: https://github.com/redwood-inference/runtime/issues/432
keith: can you paste the snippet here first? i'll quick-review before you push the PR
oliver: sure — draft below, feel free to nit:
```python
# python SDK minimal tool-calling + schema example
from redwood import RedwoodClient
client = RedwoodClient()
response = client.call_tool(
    name="calculate_totals",
    input={"items": [{"id": "sku_1", "qty": 2}]},
    structured_output={
        "type": "json_schema",
        "schema": {"type":"object","properties":{"total":{"type":"number"}},"required":["total"]}
    }
)
# response.output -> validated JSON (or schema error)
```
```js
// js SDK minimal example
import { RedClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const c = new RedClient();
const res = await c.callTool({
  name: 'calculate_totals',
  input: { items: [{ id: 'sku_1', qty: 2 }] },
  structuredOutput: {
    type: 'json_schema',
    schema: { type: 'object', properties: { total: { type: 'number' } }, required: ['total'] }
  }
});
// res.output is validated JSON or contains errors field
```
sana: looks good, add a one-liner about how to handle validation errors (retry, fallback to regex, or return schema errors upstream). example: `if res.errors: log + fallback_to_text_parser()`
oliver: will do. also fixing two links: 1) 'tool calling guide' previously pointed to old internal slug — switching to /docs/tool-calling/ 2) structured output anchor had a typo. replacing both in docs index
docs-bot: PR opened by oliver: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1756 — review requested from @sana @keith :eyes:
keith: quick nit — prefer `structured_output` key in python but `structuredOutput` in js to match SDK style guide; mention that in migration note
andrea: re: streaming note — add a short snippet showing `buffer_full_response=True` option or calling endpoint with `stream=false` for critical validations
oliver: adding both. will push updated branch in 20m. tagging @support on the PR for visibility :mailbox_with_mail:
sana: thanks — once merged can we add a migration notice to the changelog and backport to stable branch? some E2E customers are pinned
oliver: yes, i'll open a follow-up PR for the stable branch backport if needed after merge
keith: if you want, i can quick run the snippets through the SDK linter after you push
oliver: that'd be awesome. thanks all :rocket:
